import scene_landscape_update.dl

to get [a website Farm landscape for] {a pointer to website farm world:world}:
    set result to storage for one slot initialized with (a new website Farm landscape)
    set result's library to a website farm art library
    set result's objects to an empty list of a pointer to UI scene object
    set result's tiles to storage for 400 slots initialized with (a new website Farm tile scenery)
    prepare website Farm landscape templates result
    loop index from 0 to 400:
        set scenery to result's tiles + index
        set scenery's ground to a website Farm object named (formatted "ground-{index}") using (result's ground model) in result
        set scenery's crop key to -1
    set library to the address of (result's library)
    set result's barn to a website Farm object named "barn" using (a Farm house with library) in result
    set result's compost to a website Farm object named "compost" using (a Farm compost bin with library) in result
    set material to a Farm art material colored [184,200,166]
    set model to a website Farm scene model using (the Farm shape named "plane" in library) colored material casting shadow false
    set floor to a website Farm object named "floor" using model in result
    set floor's pickable to false
    set pose to a Farm art pose at [0.0,-0.72,0.0] sized [250.0,250.0,1.0] turned [-1.5707963267948966,0.0,0.0]
    set UI scene root pose in (floor's instance) to pose
    set material to a Farm art material colored [102,93,66]
    set model to a website Farm scene model using (the Farm shape named "box" in library) colored material casting shadow true
    set base to a website Farm object named "base" using model in result
    set base's pickable to false
    place website Farm object base at (a UI scene vector from [0.0,-0.54,0.0]) sized [20.08,0.25,20.08]
    update website Farm landscape result from world
    return result

to [close website Farm landscape] {a pointer to website Farm landscape:landscape}:
    for each object in (landscape's objects):
        close UI scene object object
    free landscape's objects
    loop index from 0 to 400:
        destroy the value at (landscape's tiles + index)
    deallocate landscape's tiles
    destroy the value at landscape
    deallocate landscape
